{
  "name": "Singularity Compressor",
  "icon": "theoreticalsciences:concept_compressor",
  "category": "theoreticalsciences:endgame",
  "sortnum": 64,
  "pages": [
    {
      "type": "patchouli:spotlight",
      "item": "theoreticalsciences:concept_compressor",
      "title": "Conceptual Singularity Compressor",
      "text": "Log: the $(item)Conceptual Singularity Compressor$() takes whole stacks of everything a field of science has produced and compresses them into a single singularity of pure concept.$(br2)$(thing)Tier 6$() machine."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Too complex for any crafting grid. I built this controller on the $(item)Femtoscale Assembly Line$() - check JEI for the exact parts; I needed every one of them."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Each recipe eats whole stacks: nine slots of a field's products plus three tanks. Nothing here waits on a timer - it only costs what it costs. I fed it a decade of lab notes and it handed me back one glowing point."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "The Omniscience Catalyst is made in the $(item)Extreme Assembly Table$() from every singularity there is. Here, with cosmic neutronium or transfinite coils, catalysts are forged into $(item)Omnium$() in bulk - 128 catalysts and stacks of the late metals for one ingot, or 4 ingots from 128 with transfinite coils - with no 9x9 grid to fill by hand."
    },
